{
  "ranking": [
    {
      "id": "patch_0517c5c2c927",
      "failure_port": "input_axis_tready",
      "source_line": 5049,
      "mechanism": "The failure occurs at cycle 8 where input_axis_tready is 0 but expected 1, and output_axis_tlast is 0 but expected 1. The reset logic at line 5049 unconditionally clears input_axis_tready_reg on rst. The edit '(input_axis_tready_reg) && (!rst)' at line 5049 preserves ready assertion during reset deassertion transitions, directly addressing the cycle-8 ready dropout observed in the trace."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_4f3a96077aa5",
      "failure_port": "input_axis_tready",
      "source_line": 5049,
      "mechanism": "Same failing port (input_axis_tready) and source line (5049) as above. The edit '(input_axis_tready_reg) && (!rst)' keeps the ready register asserted when rst is low, preventing the spurious deassertion at cycle 8 that causes the observed mismatch. This variant is ranked second only because the patch family appears later in the evidence list, not due to differing mechanism."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_6b110907b92c",
      "failure_port": "input_axis_tready",
      "source_line": 7213,
      "mechanism": "In STATE_IDLE when CYCLE_COUNT==1, the code sets input_axis_tready_next = output_axis_tready_int_early only if the CYCLE_COUNT==1 branch is taken. The edit at line 7213 changes the branch guard to '(CYCLE_COUNT == 1) && (input_axis_tvalid)', ensuring the ready assignment only occurs when a valid input word is present. This prevents asserting ready on invalid cycles, which aligns with the cycle-8 expectation of ready=1 only when valid data exists."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_cfc8ea21a9a5",
      "failure_port": "input_axis_tready",
      "source_line": 5809,
      "mechanism": "At line 5809 in the EXPAND_BUS idle path, input_axis_tready_next is set to 1 unconditionally after seeing input_axis_tvalid. The edit '(EXPAND_BUS) && (input_axis_tvalid)' qualifies the EXPAND_BUS condition with the valid signal, ensuring the state machine only enters the transfer sequence when valid data is actually present. This matches the trace where cycle 8 expects ready=1 (valid present) but the design may have taken a path assuming valid without checking."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_f007f011176d",
      "failure_port": "input_axis_tready",
      "source_line": 7213,
      "mechanism": "In the CYCLE_COUNT==1 branch, the ready assignment uses output_axis_tready_int_early. The edit '(input_axis_tvalid) && (!output_axis_tready_int)' at line 7213 adds a dependency on output_axis_tready_int being low, which prevents the input side from asserting ready when the output pipeline is already holding data. This directly addresses the backpressure requirement cited in the profile and the cycle-8 mismatch where ready should be 1 but the output may not be ready."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_1a6508cab211",
      "failure_port": "input_axis_tready",
      "source_line": 5809,
      "mechanism": "The EXPAND_BUS idle path at line 5809 sets input_axis_tready_next = 1 and later gates state transitions on input_axis_tlast. The edit '(EXPAND_BUS) && (!input_axis_tlast)' qualifies the condition with !tlast, ensuring that non-last words keep the pipeline flowing. The trace shows cycle 8 expects output_axis_tlast=1 but got 0, suggesting the last-word detection fired early; this edit delays last-word handling until tlast is actually asserted."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_86feac8aac1d",
      "failure_port": "input_axis_tready",
      "source_line": 5809,
      "mechanism": "Same source line (5809) as above but with opposite polarity: '(EXPAND_BUS) && (input_axis_tlast)'. This would only assert ready when tlast is high, which contradicts the need to keep ready high for non-last words. It is ranked lower because the failure shows ready should be 1 at cycle 8 (non-last context), so gating on tlast would worsen the mismatch."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_31ff37e82a23",
      "failure_port": "input_axis_tready",
      "source_line": 10177,
      "mechanism": "In STATE_TRANSFER_OUT for EXPAND_BUS, the state_next logic at line 10177 uses EXPAND_BUS to decide whether to return to TRANSFER_OUT or go IDLE. The edit '(EXPAND_BUS) && (!output_axis_tready_int)' adds a dependency on output not being ready, which would stall the state machine when backpressure exists. This aligns with the profile's backpressure requirement but the failure is at cycle 8 in what appears to be an IDLE/TRANSFER_IN boundary, making this edit less directly connected to the observed mismatch."
    }
  ]
  ,
  "explanation": "The first two patches (patch_0517c5c2c927 and patch_4f3a96077aa5) directly modify the reset-path assignment of input_axis_tready_reg at line 5049, which is the only place the ready register is cleared on reset. The trace shows a cycle-8 dropout of ready (actual 0, expected 1) coincident with a reset deassertion window, making the reset-qualification edit the most proximate fix. The next three patches (patch_6b110907b92c, patch_cfc8ea21a9a5, patch_f007f011176d) target the CYCLE_COUNT==1 and EXPAND_BUS idle paths where ready is combinatorially assigned; they add valid/ready gating that matches the protocol's requirement to assert ready only when valid data exists and the output pipeline can accept it. The remaining patches either gate on tlast (which would suppress ready on non-last words) or act deep in the EXPAND_BUS transfer-out path, which the cycle-8 trace does not appear to reach."
}
